<article class="env-lemma" id="07TY">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/07TY">Lemma <span data-tag="07TY">67.15.1</span>.</a> Let $S$ be a scheme. Let $X$ be an algebraic space over $S$. Let $\mathcal{F}$ be a quasi-coherent $\mathcal{O}_ X$-module. Let $U$ be a scheme and let $\varphi : U \to X$ be an étale morphism. Then </p>
  <div class="equation">
  \[  \text{Supp}(\varphi ^*\mathcal{F}) = |\varphi |^{-1}(\text{Supp}(\mathcal{F}))  \]
</div>
  <p> where the left hand side is the support of $\varphi ^*\mathcal{F}$ as a quasi-coherent module on the scheme $U$. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      Let $u\in U$ be a (usual) point and let $\overline{x}$ be a geometric point lying over $u$. By Properties of Spaces, Lemma <a href="/tag/05VP" data-tag="05VP">66.29.4</a> we have $(\varphi ^*\mathcal{F})_ u \otimes _{\mathcal{O}_{U, u}} \mathcal{O}_{X, \overline{x}} = \mathcal{F}_{\overline{x}}$. Since $\mathcal{O}_{U, u} \to \mathcal{O}_{X, \overline{x}}$ is the strict henselization by Properties of Spaces, Lemma <a href="/tag/04KF" data-tag="04KF">66.22.1</a> we see that it is faithfully flat (see More on Algebra, Lemma <a href="/tag/07QM" data-tag="07QM">15.46.1</a>). Thus we see that $(\varphi ^*\mathcal{F})_ u = 0$ if and only if $\mathcal{F}_{\overline{x}} = 0$. This proves the lemma. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>